DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These functions get and set the process‐shared attribute in a mutex at‐
       tributes object.  This attribute must be appropriately  set  to  ensure
       correct,  efficient  operation of a mutex created using this attributes
       object.

       The process‐shared attribute can have one of the following values:

       PPTTHHRREEAADD__PPRROOCCEESSSS__PPRRIIVVAATTEE
              Mutexes created with this attributes object  are  to  be  shared
              only  among threads in the same process that initialized the mu‐
              tex.  This is the default value for the process‐shared mutex at‐
              tribute.

       PPTTHHRREEAADD__PPRROOCCEESSSS__SSHHAARREEDD
              Mutexes created with this attributes object can  be  shared  be‐
              tween  any threads that have access to the memory containing the
              object, including threads in different processes.

       pptthhrreeaadd__mmuutteexxaattttrr__ggeettppsshhaarreedd() places the value of  the  process‐shared
       attribute of the mutex attributes object referred to by _a_t_t_r in the lo‐
       cation pointed to by _p_s_h_a_r_e_d.

       pptthhrreeaadd__mmuutteexxaattttrr__sseettppsshhaarreedd() sets the value of the process‐shared at‐
       tribute of the mutex attributes object referred to by _a_t_t_r to the value
       specified in ppsshhaarreedd.

       If  _a_t_t_r  does not refer to an initialized mutex attributes object, the
       behavior is undefined.

